 "explanation": "The neuron fires weakly and diffusely across narrative prose rather than on any specific semantic content. Its most consistent tendency is activation on structural \"glue\" tokens at clause and sentence boundaries: sentence-initial connectives (After, Until, If, Can, For), conjunctions and prepositions (and, with, to, as, by), punctuation (periods, commas, quotation marks), plus occasional mid-word subword fragments. The contexts are mostly storytelling or expository text (fan fiction, true-crime narrative, summaries), suggesting a general narrative-continuation feature rather than a topical one.",
